Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] mm/vmscan: keep the watermark boost out of the direct reclaim throttle

Goes with 0002 (watermark boost no longer applies to the min watermark).

throttle_direct_reclaim() puts a task that enters direct reclaim to sleep
while free memory in the zones up to ZONE_NORMAL is at or below half of the
"pfmemalloc reserve". allow_direct_reclaim() sums that reserve with
min_wmark_pages(), which includes zone->watermark_boost.

With 0002, ordinary allocations enter direct reclaim only below the real
(unboosted) min watermark. Whenever the boost of a zone is larger than its
min watermark, half of (min + boost) is above min, so a task entering direct
reclaim while a boost is active is throttled until kswapd has lifted free
memory above that line (sleeping without timeout for __GFP_FS requests, up
to 1 s otherwise). pgscan_direct_throttle in /proc/vmstat counts these.

Use the unboosted min watermark for the reserve, as 0002 does in
zone_watermark_fast().

Compile-tested only (7.3.4 and 7.4-rc1). Not run. Check pgscan_direct_throttle
before and after under memstress to see whether this path is hit at all.
---
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -6957,7 +6957,7 @@
 		if (!zone_reclaimable_pages(zone) && zone_page_state_snapshot(zone, NR_FREE_PAGES))
 			continue;
 
-		pfmemalloc_reserve += min_wmark_pages(zone);
+		pfmemalloc_reserve += zone->_watermark[WMARK_MIN];
 		free_pages += zone_page_state_snapshot(zone, NR_FREE_PAGES);
 	}
 
